claim.claim-text:
receiving, via an interface, at least one frame and removing a first header from the at least one frame to produce at least one stripped frame;
associating, based on a carrier identifier included in the at least one stripped frame, an adaptive coding and modulation (ACM) tagged frame included in the at least one stripped frame with a carrier corresponding to the carrier identifier;
extracting a baseband frame included in the ACM tagged frame;
modulating the baseband frame onto the carrier to generate a modulated signal; and
generating, based on the modulated signal, a filtered baseband signal.

receiving, via an interface, at least one frame and removing a first header from the at least one frame to produce at least one stripped frame;
associating, based on a carrier identifier included in the at least one stripped frame, an adaptive coding and modulation (ACM) tagged frame included in the at least one stripped frame with a carrier corresponding to the carrier identifier;
extracting a baseband frame included in the ACM tagged frame;
modulating the baseband frame onto the carrier to generate a modulated signal;
generating, based on the modulated signal, a filtered baseband signal;
causing transmission of a radio frequency (RF) signal corresponding to the filtered baseband signal;
demodulating one or more carriers in an intermediate frequency (IF) band; and
extracting one or more streams of frames corresponding to the one or more carriers.
